From: lain3d <eyeofsteiner@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] soc: qcom: pmic_glink_altmode: make PAN_EN optional

Diagnostic patch, not proposed for upstream as-is.

ALTMODE_PAN_EN is where Linux announces itself to charger_pd and asks to be told
about Type-C port state. charger_pd runs on the ADSP, is started by firmware
long before Linux, and already owns the port. Everything downstream - the
per-port USBC_NOTIFY_IND, pmic_glink_altmode_worker(), the PAN_ACK - follows
from that one request.

On a Surface Pro 11 (X1E80100) booting from a USB-C disk, the root filesystem
intermittently dies 14.9-16.3ms after the notification arrives, across three
independent failures:

  usb 4-1: cmd cmplt err -71
  sd 0:0:0:0: [sda] FAILED Result: hostbyte=DID_NO_CONNECT

Nothing on the Linux side touches the hardware in that window. The ps8830
retimer reports "no change, not touching the chip" and the QMP combo PHY reports
"already in mode 2, not touching the PHY"; USB_QUIRK_NO_LPM does not prevent it
either. Blacklisting qcom_q6v5_pas so Linux never attaches to the ADSP gave ten
consecutive clean boots.

That last result removes the ADSP entirely, which also costs the CDSP, battery
reporting and any prospect of audio. This parameter separates the two questions:
the ADSP attaches normally and everything else it serves comes back, but Linux
never joins the PD conversation.

  pmic_glink_altmode.pan_enable=0

Cost when disabled: no Type-C port notifications, so no USB-C DisplayPort alt
mode and no orientation/mux updates from firmware. The DP HPD bridges are still
allocated at probe, so the MSM display component driver still binds.

Signed-off-by: lain3d <eyeofsteiner@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -30,6 +30,19 @@
 #define ALTMODE_PAN_EN		0x10
+
+/*
+ * PAN_EN is where Linux announces itself to charger_pd, which is already
+ * running on the ADSP and already owns the port. On a machine whose root
+ * filesystem hangs off that port, joining the conversation has been observed
+ * to drop the USB link ~15ms later. Allow it to be suppressed so the ADSP can
+ * still be attached for everything else it serves.
+ */
+static bool pan_enable = true;
+module_param(pan_enable, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(pan_enable,
+		 "Request Type-C port notifications from the remote (default 1)");
+
 #define ALTMODE_PAN_ACK		0x11

@@ -545,6 +558,15 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_enable_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 	struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmode = work_to_altmode(work);
 	int ret;

+	if (!pan_enable) {
+		dev_info(altmode->dev,
+			 "pan_enable=0, not requesting altmode notifications\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	dev_info(altmode->dev, "requesting altmode notifications (PAN_EN)\n");
+
 	ret = pmic_glink_altmode_request(altmode, ALTMODE_PAN_EN, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(altmode->dev, "failed to request altmode notifications: %d\n", ret);
